    "_comment": [
      "Two-parameter CPM setup (.plans/cpm_setup_proposal_2026-09-19.md Addendum 2),",
      "with tol_init set from the measured sweep rather than the shipped 10.0.",
      "",
      "tol_init 0.1: the bandwidth walks down from tol_init at a bounded rate, so an",
      "expensive run ends inside the transient. At 10.0 the schedule reached only",
      "0.0041 in 13,000 evaluations -- 68x above the k-th order statistic its own",
      "draws supported -- and the weak parameter contracted 58%. At 0.1 it reaches",
      "2x the order statistic and contracts 81-84% with coverage intact. 0.1 is",
      "about 1/5 of this benchmark's prior-predictive median discrepancy (0.459);",
      "0.01 is no better and less consistent. Jobs 14262028/29/30.",
      "",
      "tol_init is shared by both arms of the matched comparison by construction, so",
      "this favours neither method.",
      "",
      "The in-harness rejection_abc arm is rank_parallel -- one rank per replicate --",
      "so on this expensive simulator it gets 1/48th of the machine and ~240",
      "evaluations. The FAIR rejection baseline is diag_cpm_prior_corpus.py at 48",
      "ranks and a matched evaluation count (job 14262032): 91%/67% contraction at",
      "tolerance 0.0029, against the async arm's 0.000061. Report that one."
    ],
